Partly. An smtp handler does get the mail as an Amazon SES-shaped object at `Records[0].ses`, next to the portable `event.data` (from, to, cc, subject, text, html, headers, attachments). But the smtp trigger is on premises only, so it needs an on-premises deployment, not Tencent.

```python
def handler(event, ctx):
    if event.type != "smtp":
        return None
    mail = event.data
    return {"subject": mail["subject"], "from": mail["from"]}
```
